melody:
# Refrain as published in 1927 ("Very slow"); the last phrase is the high one printed in the score
Ol' man riv-er, that ol' man riv-er,
Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4 C4/ Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4
he must know some-thing, but don't say noth-ing,
F4/ G4 G4 F4/ Eb4 F4/ G4 Bb4 C5/ Bb4
he just keeps roll-ing, he keeps on roll-ing a-long.
C5/ Bb4 Bb4 G4/ F4 G4/ Bb4 Bb4 G4/ F4 G4/ Eb4(4) ~Eb4(2) ~Eb4 r/
He don't plant ta-ters, he don't plant cot-ton,
Bb3/ Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4 C4/ Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4
and them that plants 'em is soon for-got-ten;
F4/ G4 Bb4 C5/ Bb4 C5/ Eb5 Eb5 D5/ C5
but ol' man riv-er he just keeps roll-ing a-long.
D5/ Bb4 Bb4 G4/ F4 G4/ Bb4 Bb4 G4/ F4 G4/ Eb4(4) ~Eb4 r r(2)
You and me, we sweat and strain,
D5 Bb4 C5. Eb5/ D5 Bb4 C5(2)
bo-dy all ach-ing and racked with pain.
D5/. D5// Bb4 C5/. C5// Eb5 D5 Bb4 C5(2)
"Tote that barge!" "Lift that bale!"
Bb4/ r/ G4 A4(2) Bb4 G4 A4(2)
Git a lit-tle drunk and you land in jail.
Bb4/. Bb4// G4/. G4// A4 C5/. C5// Bb4 G4 F4(2)
Ah gits wea-ry and sick of try-in',
Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4 C4/ Bb3 Bb3 C4/ Eb4
Ah'm tired of liv-in' and skeered of dy-in',
F4/ G4 Bb4 C5/ Bb4 C5/ Eb5 Eb5 F5/ Eb5
but ol' man riv-er he just keeps roll-ing a-long.
F5/ G5 G5 F5/ Eb5 F5/ G5 G5 F5/ Eb5/ F5 Eb5(4) ~Eb5 r r(2)
